  "geometric_identity": {
    "chart": "The cylinder has transverse y. In either turned head use signed (1+v); extend through the rim by the same signed inward offset in its normal collar. Before the cap collar runs out switch to the regular cap (x,z) coordinates, including the center. The inverse takes the true original profile offset ray. Transform a tangent Jacobi map by Dq_new/Dq_old from the two reference tangent frames and record the point, tangent and velocity gaps.",
    "material": "For T containing the two corrected tangents as rows and G=T T^T, subtract the metric derivative from the differentiated normal equations to obtain Dw=G^-1((DT)A+T(DA)-(DG)w), where w=G^-1 T A. Add the true X0 and its derivatives. Integrate q dot = -X and J dot = -DX J on the entire [0,pi].",
    "comparison": "Relative generalized eigenvalues compare the rotated, marked world tangent R_t DF(q(t)) J + e_z db(q0) with exactly the initially frozen candidate target at q0. The upper marks lie in the invariant material subdisk with chi=0 and exact positive polar X0; their spatial supports remain on the original flat region. The relative spectrum is independent of initial regular chart.",
    "interpretation": "Each result is a sampled floating-point trajectory comparison. Both tolerances report independent function evaluations, crossings and residuals, plus actual partial errors. No uniform flow, global embedding, reach or strict lower bound follows from the numerical report."
  },
